	Missions are the crown jewel of the Nova datafile, as well as the largest and most complex resources in the game. Each misn resource corresponds to a single mission that the player can undertake, with the name of the mission (which the player sees in the mission list) being the name of the associated misn resource. The first six fields in a misn resource help Nova determine where and when the mission is available:\
\

\f2\i \ul AvailStel:			Which planets the mission is available at:
\f1\i0 \ulnone \
	\cf2 -1			Any inhabited stellar\cf0 \
\
	128-2175		ID number of a specific stellar\
\
	\cf2 5000-7047		Stellar in a system adjacent to specific system\cf0 \
\
	9999-10255		Specific govt's stellar\
\
	\cf2 15000-15255	Specific govt's ally's stellar\cf0 \
\
	20000-20255	Stellar of anybody but this specific govt\
\
	\cf2 25000-25255	Specific govt's enemy's stellar\cf0 \
\
	30000-30255	Stellar of specific govt or any of its class mates\
\
	\cf2 31000-31255	Stellar not of specific govt nor of any of its class mates\cf0 \
\

\f2\i \ul AvailLoc:	Where on a planet this mission is available:
\f1\i0 \ulnone \
	\cf2 0	From the mission computer\cf0 \
	1	In the bar\
	\cf2 2	Offered from ship (must set up associated p\'91rs resource as well)\cf0 \
	3	In the main spaceport dialog\
	\cf2 4	In the trading dialog\cf0 \
	5	In the shipyard dialog\
	\cf2 6	In the outfit dialog\cf0 \
\
\
AvailRecord		What your legal record in this system must be for this mission to become available\
	0            ignored\
		pos. value   record must be at least this high\
		neg. value   record must be at least this low\
	-32000       when the player has dominated the stellar in question\
	-32001       when the player has dominated at least one stellar\
\
AvailRating		What your combat rating must be for this mission to be available:\
	-1	ignored\
	0+	rating must be at least this high\
\
AvailRandom	A randomization factor, to ensure that some missions aren't available all the time. Mission randomizing values are recalculated each time you warp into a system. \
	100          always available\
	1-99         available this % of the time\
\
\
The next two fields in the misn resource define where the player needs to go to\
complete the mission:\
\

\f2\i \cf3 \ul TravelStel\cf0 	\cf2 Which stellar object the player must go to during the mission
\f1\i0 \ulnone \
\cf0 	\cf3 -1		\cf2 	No specific stellar destination\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 -2		\cf2 	A random inhabited stellar\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 -3		\cf2 	A random uninhabited planet\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 128-2175	\cf2 	ID number of a specific stellar (note that the mission travel objectives will also be fulfilled when landing on a duplicate stellar that has the idendical name and coordinates to the stellar you specify here)\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 9999-10255		\cf2 Random stellar of a specific govt\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 15000-15255	\cf2 Random stellar of a specific govt's ally\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 20000-20255	\cf2 Random stellar of anybody but this specific govt\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 25000-25255	\cf2 Random stellar of specific govt's enemy\
\cf0 \
	\cf3 30000-30255	\cf2 Random stellar of specific govt or any of its class mates\cf0 \
\
	\cf3 31000-31255\cf0 	\cf2 Random stellar not of specific govt nor of any of its class mates\cf0 \
\
\
ReturnStel		Where the player must return to in order to complete the mission and receive payment:\
\cf2 	-1		No specific stellar destination\
\cf0 \
	-2		A random inhabited stellar\
\
	\cf2 -3		A random uninhabited stellar\cf0 \
\
	-4		The initial stellar, where the mission was accepted\
\
	\cf2 128-2175	ID number of a specific stellar (note that the mission will also complete when landing on a duplicate stellar that has the idendical name and coordinates to the stellar you specify here)\cf0 \
\
	9999-10255		Random stellar of a specific govt\
\
	\cf2 15000-15255	Random stellar of a specific govt's ally\
\cf0 \
	20000-20255	Random stellar of anybody but this specific govt\
\
	\cf2 25000-25255	Random stellar of specific govt's enemy\cf0 \
\
	30000-30255	Random stellar of specific govt or any of its class mates\
\
	\cf2 31000-31255	Random stellar not of specific govt nor of any of its class mates\cf0 \
