\f2\i \ul Flags:	Descriptions:
\f1\i0 \ulnone \
\cf2 0x0001         Marks the mission as an auto-aborting mission, which will automatically abort itself after it is accepted. (sometimes useful to create special ships) Any control bits pointed to by the mission\'d5s CompBitSet fields will be automatically set when the mission aborts.  Note: there must be special ships associated with the mission to trigger the auto-abort.  If the mission is one in which a special ship replaces a p\'91rs ship at mission start (such as for a "rescue disabled ship" mission) and the SpecialShipGoal is 2 or 5 (board or rescue) the mission will auto-abort after the special ship is boarded.\cf0 \
0x0002	Don\'d5t show the red destination arrows on the map\
\
\cf2 0x0004	Can\'d5t refuse the mission\cf0 \
\
0x0008	Mission takes away 100 units of fuel upon auto-abort. (mission won't be offered if player has less than 100 units of fuel)\
\
\cf2 0x0010	Infinite auxShips\cf0 \
\
0x0020	Mission fails if you're scanned\
\
\cf2 0x0040	Apply -5x CompReward reversal on abort\cf0 \
\
0x0080	Global penalty when jettisoning mission cargo in space (currently ignored)\
\
\cf2 0x0100	Show green arrow on map in initial briefing\cf0 \
\
0x0200	Show an additional arrow on the map for the ShipSyst\
\
\cf2 0x0400	Mission is invisible and won't appear in the mission info dialog. (be careful with this!)\cf0 \
\
0x0800	The special ships' type will be selected at mission start and then kept the same whenever the special ships for that mission are created, until the mission ends. This can be used for (e.g.) "attack pirate" missions where you want the type of the enemy ship to be random at first but you don't want it to change every time the player lands or re-enters the system.\
\
\cf2 0x2000	Mission unavailable if player\'d5s ship is of inherentAI type 1 or 2  (cargo ships)\cf0 \
\
0x4000	Mission unavailable if player\'d5s ship is of inherentAI type 3 or 4  (warships)\
\
\cf2 0x8000	Mission will fail if player is boarded by pirates.\cf0 \
\
\

